# Provide Markdown (.md) format description of changes introduce by the MR

All outputs must be wrapped in markdown code blocks for easy copy-paste.
Outputs should be as concise as possible, without sacrificing clarity.

## get Branch commit activity report

```bash
git --no-pager log $(git merge-base origin/main HEAD)..HEAD \
  --pretty=format:'{"hash":"%H","author":"%an","date":"%ad","subject":"%s","body":"%b"}' \
  --date=iso --reverse
```

## Slack message (French)

Provide a bullet-point summary in French, highlighting the key changes of the MR.
Tone should be suitable for internal communication in a technical Slack channel.

## MR (English)

### MR title

Generate a single-line, concise, and descriptive title suitable for the merge request.

### MR description

Provide a bullet-point list (in English) summarizing the MR.
Structure and content should mirror the Slack summary, but phrased for formal use in a merge request.
